A||||8||86SE||HELP!!  4 cyl has a spark and fuel, but no go!!||||5||
Z||000000||86SE||05-31-2000||11:24 PM||||I have been workin a 84 4cyl Fiero.  It has 199995.7 miles, it gets fuel and im sure it has a spark.<P>I can see the main injector on the carb shoot gas into the carb.  And I took out the all the spark plugs and turned it over and all 4 of em sparked.  But 2 plugs were wet.<P>I have tried adjusting the timeing and I got it to just barely fire.  It feels like it will fire, just not quite.<P>There is also a smell of fuel from the exhaust tips after i crank on it.  And after it feels like it will start, white smoke comes from the distributor (smells like burnt fuel).<P>Any help will be greatly appreciated!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||06-01-2000||12:15 AM||||Fuel, spark, and compression, two out of three won't do it.<BR>Was everything just fine until it up and quit working one day?<BR>Get the timing back close to where it should be and tow the car in second gear until about 1500 RPM.  This is fast enough to overcome almost zero compression.<BR>If this starts it and the battery won't then my two cents is on compression.<BR>Unlit gasoline vapor is white. Was it really coming out the distributor or was that a typo?||||reg||12
Z||000002||86SE||06-01-2000||12:25 AM||||opps!! I meant 119 thousand miles!!  Yeah, one day it just up and quit and wouldent start.  I replaced the blown 10 AMP ECM fuse started to work on gettin it started but so far it wont.  The smoke looks like its coming in the vacinity of the distributor.<P>Is it possible to tow an Automatic to get the RPMs up??||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||06-01-2000||02:07 AM||||has the car been sitting for a while?  Try adding heat, or some gas treatment if it has.<P>Also, see if the IAC is moving, take the aircleaner off, and someone turn the key on, and you should see the little cone move.||||reg||1
Z||000004||86SE||06-01-2000||02:20 AM||||Its been sittin since about December.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierospeeder||06-01-2000||05:11 AM||||if the tank is very low, you can get one of those pump siphons to drain it into a gas container.   Or you can fill the gas tank up with fresh gas, and add some heat, and or some gas additive to remove water and dirt.<P>I bought a motorcycle, and the previous owner had it sitting outside, and it got wet from the rain.  I couldn't get it to start.  I drained the floats, and it started.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fotofrank||06-01-2000||01:42 PM||||The big tip here is the blown 10 amp fuse. Did the car start after you replaced the fuse? If not trace the power and ground for that 10 amp ECM fuse and it just may be the ECM or something directly related.Best bet is removeal of the 10 amp ECM fuse and try to start the car. If the simtoms do not change the ECM is most likely the problem.<BR>Best of luck and report the fix to the forum.||||reg||8
Z||000007||86SE||06-01-2000||02:35 PM||||The 10 AMP fuse was the ECM fuse.  Who ever messed with the car before I did cut the two wires the goto the TBI unit.  Then he put them back together with out using electrical tape!  So the wires were just grounding on the fuel line causing it to blow a fuse.<P>I pulled that same fuse out on my 86 SE, and the car ran, then quit.  It has the same effect as pulling the fuel pump fuse, the fuel pump does dont pump the fuel.||||reg||1
Z||000008||86SE||06-01-2000||03:19 PM||||Hey wait a minute, I forgot to mention the ECMs codes.  It gets a code 33 or 34 for the MAP sensor.  The MAP sensor controls the ignition timing and fuel delivery doesnt it?<P>I'll switch the bad one from the 4cyl with mine from my v-6 and see if it starts.||||reg||3
